OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Police investigating the disappearance
OL,6, of confidential information from a
OL,7, Belfast police station now say that two
OL,8, documents have gone missing.
OL,10,FIt was thought that only one document
OL,11,Fhad disappeared when it was discovered
OL,12,Flast Thursday that a locked cabinet in
OL,13,FDunmurray station had been forced open.
OL,15,FThe documents, in the form of
OL,16,Fphotographic montages, contain a total
OL,17,Fof 29 photographs of terrorist suspects
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 19-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789772636
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/22
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A confidential document containing the
OL,6, names and photographs of 18 IRA
OL,7, suspects has been presented at an SDLP
OL,8, news conference in Belfast.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FDeputy SDLP leader Mr Seamus Mallon
OL,11,Fsaid the document had leaked from a
OL,12,FBelfast police station to the loyalist
OL,13,Fterrorist organisation, the UVF.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FHe said it was given by a UVF member to
OL,16,Fthe UDA Protestant paramilitary group,
OL,17,Fwho passed it on to a nationalist man.
OL,19,FMr Mallon said he had already informed
OL,20,Fthe police about the document and would
OL,21,Fco-operate fully in any inquiry.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 19-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789772636
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/22
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, A security document with the names of
OL,6, 18 IRA suspects has been handed to SDLP
OL,7, deputy leader Mr Seamus Mallon.
OL,9,FMr Mallon said the document had been
OL,10,Fgiven to one of his constituents by a
OL,11,Fmember of a loyalist terrorist group
OL,12,Flast August.
OL,14,FThe man who was not on the list and not
OL,15,Fa member of the IRA or Sinn Fein had
OL,16,Fwaited until now to make the matter
OL,17,Fpublic because of fears for his safety.
OL,19,FOne of the men on the list was killed
OL,20,Flast year when a bomb he was preparing
OL,21,Fexploded prematurely.
OL,23,T]CFrom 19-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
